WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.434
-Thank you so much
for coming on.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:03.868
-I could not be happier.
I'm so excited to be here.

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:04.868
-We're so happy that
you're here.

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:05.901
-Thank you.

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:08.400
-Congrats on the film
"Purple Hearts."

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.734
You worked so hard on this film.
It comes out on Netflix.

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:13.100
And not just comes out.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.267
It's the number-1 film,
globally, out of all Netflix.

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:18.067
I mean, it's the
biggest movie out there.

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:19.734
And you're all -- It's all you.

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:21.234
Your fingerprints are
all over this.

00:00:21.234 --> 00:00:23.200
You're in the soundtrack.
You star in it.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.367
You're funny.
You're awesome in it.

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:28.334
It's the biggest thing.
How do you feel?

00:00:28.334 --> 00:00:30.400
-I was talking to my mom the
other night about all of this

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:34.601
and I realized that I can't find
a word to describe how I feel.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:38.567
I'm just so overjoyed
and overwhelmed and grateful.

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:40.901
And, you know, I poured my heart
and soul into this film,

00:00:40.901 --> 00:00:42.634
and for it to be
loved by the world

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:45.634
as deeply as I loved making it
is just incredible.

00:00:45.634 --> 00:00:46.667
-Good for you.
-Thank you.

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:47.801
How did --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:47.801 --> 00:00:49.868
-Thank you.

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:52.400
-Explain to me, how does the
movie -- how did it come about?

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.234
-So, about five years ago, I was
shooting a show in Portland

00:00:55.234 --> 00:00:56.934
called "Pretty Little Liars:
The perfectionists."

00:00:56.934 --> 00:00:59.801
And my incredible director,
Liz Allen --

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:02.467
she approached me around
Christmastime with a script

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:04.033
and she said,
"Merry early Christmas."

00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:05.634
And it said "'Purple Hearts.'"

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:07.434
And it was a rough draft
of this movie.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:09.467
And she said that she wanted to
embark on this journey

00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:11.667
as more than just
actor and director,

00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:13.667
but as partners and producers.

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:15.400
And that's how
the journey began.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.667
And five years later,
after shooting the film,

00:01:17.667 --> 00:01:19.601
writing the soundtrack,
producing it, here we are.

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:21.367
And it's just been
the most incredible journey.

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:22.634
-But, I mean, kind of
perfect for you

00:01:22.634 --> 00:01:25.234
because you're a great singer
and a great actor.

00:01:25.234 --> 00:01:26.400
-Do you actually
want to know how she

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.467
wanted to work with me again?

00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:28.701
-Yeah.

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:30.267
-I was in the middle of
the woods in Portland,

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:31.701
shooting a dramatic scene.

00:01:31.701 --> 00:01:34.701
And before I did my
dramatic scenes at the time,

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:36.601
I had to sing a song.

00:01:36.601 --> 00:01:38.501
And "Star is Born"
had just come out.

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:41.400
And I was belting -- and I
thought no one could hear me --

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.667
the ending song,
"I'll Never Love Again."

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:45.701
And she was like --
She overheard this crazy girl

00:01:45.701 --> 00:01:47.067
in the middle of the woods
belting "I'll Never Love Again"

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:48.501
and she's like,
"I have to work with her."

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:50.267
-"I have to find who this is."
-She's like, "Who is this girl!"

00:01:50.267 --> 00:01:51.267
-"Oh, my gosh.
What are you doing?"

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:52.267
And she goes -- Yeah.

00:01:52.267 --> 00:01:54.000
-I'm so grateful
for that moment.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.834
-Thank you, Gaga.
Yeah, there you go.

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:57.200
-Thank you.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:00.601
-Have you always wanted to
sing and act since you remember?

00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:02.467
-I don't remember
ever not wanting to do this.

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:04.534
It's so much more
than what I do.

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:06.667
It's who I am.
-And a very supportive mom, too.

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:09.234
I got to meet
your beautiful mom backstage.

00:02:09.234 --> 00:02:10.400
-She's my everything.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:11.634
She's here
in the audience tonight.

00:02:11.634 --> 00:02:13.167
So, thank you, Mom.
-Yeah.

00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:15.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:17.667
Good job, Mom.

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:20.567
For anyone who hasn't seen
"Purple Hearts" yet,

00:02:20.567 --> 00:02:21.968
can you set it up for everyone?

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:26.400
-Yeah, so, "Purple Hearts,"
to me, is a love story,

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:27.934
but it's so much more than
a love story.

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:32.467
It's a story about two people,
two hearts from opposite worlds,

00:02:32.467 --> 00:02:34.601
one red, one blue, who were
raised to hate each other,

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:37.100
who, through the power of love,
they come together

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:38.667
and form a beautiful shade
of purple.

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:41.334
And if love can do this
with two hearts,

00:02:41.334 --> 00:02:43.133
it's what the world
needs now more than ever.

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:45.701
-Yeah, that is exactly right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:45.701 --> 00:02:46.868
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:49.334
Here's Sofia Carson in
"Purple Hearts."

00:02:49.334 --> 00:02:50.701
Take a look at this.

00:02:50.701 --> 00:02:52.601
-Alright, I, uh -- I get this.

00:02:52.601 --> 00:02:54.667
-What do you get?
-You.

00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:55.934
Yeah.
-Me?

00:02:55.934 --> 00:02:57.534
-Yeah, yeah.
You're kind of predictable.

00:02:57.534 --> 00:02:59.067
I've -- I've
met your type before.

00:02:59.067 --> 00:03:01.400
Yeah.
-Oh, do tell.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.467
-Drive a Lexus
that your parents paid for,

00:03:03.467 --> 00:03:05.334
but it's a hybrid, so it's okay.

00:03:05.334 --> 00:03:07.767
You probably tweet a lot
about other people's rights,

00:03:07.767 --> 00:03:08.868
but when it actually
comes down --

00:03:08.868 --> 00:03:11.100
- Sorry.
It's just fascinating to me.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.801
Do you -- do you have a PhD
in mansplaining?

00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:15.133
-When it actually comes down to
fighting for these rights,

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:16.534
you don't want to
do anything, right?

00:03:16.534 --> 00:03:18.567
Because guns are mean,
and you're a pacifist.

00:03:18.567 --> 00:03:20.634
I guess it's our job to go off

00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:22.467
and fight those battles
for you, right?

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:24.567
I bet you have
a little "Peace/love" tattoo

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:25.634
on your back to prove it.

00:03:25.634 --> 00:03:27.767
-On my ass, actually,

00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:30.300
which you can't touch,
but you can kiss.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:34.934
-Oh, snap! Come on!

00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:38.868
The movie is a huge hit,

00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:41.834
and so is the soundtrack,
which you co-wrote.

00:03:41.834 --> 00:03:43.501
-Yes, with Justin Tranter.
Thank you so much.

00:03:43.501 --> 00:03:46.100
-Congrats on that.
Come on, you're doing it all.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:48.534
I just -- Not to put you on
the spot or anything,

00:03:48.534 --> 00:03:52.033
but, you know, we always
have the silver mic here.

00:03:52.033 --> 00:03:56.868
And we have the greatest band of
all late night, The Roots.

00:03:56.868 --> 00:03:59.534
Could you do a little bit of
your hit "Come Back Home"?

00:03:59.534 --> 00:04:01.267
-Are you asking me to sing
"Come Back Home"

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:02.334
with The Roots right now?

00:04:02.334 --> 00:04:04.334
-Yes.
-I would be honored.

00:04:04.334 --> 00:04:06.801
But can you sing it with me?
-Want me to?

00:04:06.801 --> 00:04:08.934
-Will you guys sing just
the very end of the song?

00:04:08.934 --> 00:04:11.734
I'll say...
♪ Come back home ♪

00:04:11.734 --> 00:04:12.801
-Yeah, we can do that.

00:04:12.801 --> 00:04:14.400
-♪ Come back home ♪

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:15.901
-There you go.
-Yeah. We got this.

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:18.434
-Okay, guys, you ready?
♪♪

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:28.868
♪ We're drowning in our eyes ♪

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:32.667
♪ Don't know what we'll find ♪

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:36.467
♪ I'm not sure,
should we fly or fight this? ♪

00:04:36.467 --> 00:04:38.434
♪ We're terrified ♪

00:04:38.434 --> 00:04:42.234
♪ Pretending now
that we don't care ♪

00:04:42.234 --> 00:04:45.501
♪ Tension cuts, cuts the air ♪

00:04:45.501 --> 00:04:47.334
♪ We're more than scared ♪

00:04:47.334 --> 00:04:50.934
♪ I'm drowning in your eyes ♪

00:04:50.934 --> 00:04:53.534
♪ I'm terrified ♪

00:04:54.868 --> 00:04:58.567
♪ Letting my fears show
till I can face 'em ♪

00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:02.167
♪ Letting my tears go
till I can taste them ♪

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:05.734
♪ How do I know
where you and I go? ♪

00:05:05.734 --> 00:05:08.400
♪ Damn it, I hope you ♪

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:11.734
♪ Come back home ♪

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:13.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:20.033
-♪ Come back home ♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:20.033 --> 00:05:21.400
Sofia Carson, everybody.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:24.033
"Purple Hearts"
is streaming now on Netflix.

00:05:24.033 --> 00:05:25.834
Lauren Spencer-Smith
performs after the break.

00:05:25.834 --> 00:05:26.968
Stick around, everybody.

